"""Draws the bar pet (a tiger cub, 16x16 pixel art) into assets/pet-ANIMAL-COAT.png, one sheet per coat.
Seven animals: the cat (tiger cub), a dog, a frog, a bird, a turtle, a fox and a dragon; all have the same twelve frames.

    assets/pet-build            # writes pet-cat-tiger.png, pet-dog-golden.png, ... next to this script
    assets/pet-build PREVIEW [cat|dog|frog|bird|turtle|fox|dragon]    # also writes PREVIEW: that animal's coats, every frame

One row of frames, each 16x16, facing right (PetSprite.qml mirrors it to face left):
  0 stand   1 stand, eyes shut   2 walk a   3 walk b   4 sit   5 asleep a   6 asleep b
  7 lying awake   8 washing   9 pounce   10 eating   11 standing, tail the other way
(the dragon's 8 is breathing fire, 9 flying with its wings up, 11 flying with them down)
Edit the grids below and run this again; Quickshell picks the new image up on reload.
"""
